            <ArticleTitle>Accordion right coronary artery: an unusual complication of PTCA guidewire entrapment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The contour of the epicardial coronary vessels may change considerably during coronary angioplasty. We report the extreme and unique &quot;accordion-like&quot; wrinkling of the mid right coronary artery as a result of distal guidewire entrapment during coronary angioplasty. Recognition of this artifact and its treatment may prevent further complications of coronary angioplasty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
